WEBVTT

00:04.900 --> 00:09.600
Four hours a day at 900 yen an hour, times 11 days...

00:09.700 --> 00:11.470
39,600 yen.

00:12.270 --> 00:14.370
Subtract the loaned printing fees,

00:14.370 --> 00:16.360
group participation fee, and miscellaneous expenses...

00:17.310 --> 00:19.810
Then, add the 7500 yen worth of savings I took out...

00:19.810 --> 00:22.180
...and the advance
I got on my allowance.

00:22.650 --> 00:25.550
From that, subtract the
Comi-Pa participation fee,

00:25.680 --> 00:30.120
printing fees for the new issue, and 2000 yen for emergency funds.

00:31.090 --> 00:33.920
It's within my budget.
I can go to Comi-Pa.

00:34.290 --> 00:36.850
Not so fast, squid gold standard!

00:37.430 --> 00:38.360
Huh? What?

00:39.400 --> 00:40.830
Gold standard!

00:40.830 --> 00:43.300
In other words, a system where the weight of gold...

00:43.300 --> 00:45.140
...is considered equal to the value of currency.

00:45.140 --> 00:46.500
No!

00:48.440 --> 00:51.410
It is too early to feel relief, my brother!

00:51.840 --> 00:53.310
The problem of a budget...

00:53.310 --> 00:56.310
...is like hanging up a good luck charm to ward off the rain...

00:56.310 --> 00:58.480
...if our endeavor was to climb Mount Fuji!

00:58.480 --> 01:02.450
Doujinshi Production Flowchart

00:58.950 --> 01:02.190
Have you forgotten that there's a ton of things to create a doujinshi?!

01:02.890 --> 01:04.150
'Morning!

01:04.920 --> 01:07.090
What's goin' on? What're ya lookin' at?

01:07.460 --> 01:09.660
Oh, is this about Comi-Pa?

01:09.660 --> 01:12.150
You sound so easy going.
How far have you gotten, Yuu?

01:12.930 --> 01:16.460
Let's see, I got ten pages of layout done last night,

01:16.600 --> 01:18.470
so I've only got a little more to go.

01:18.770 --> 01:19.570
Already?!

01:19.840 --> 01:22.140
Haste makes waste, they say.

01:22.140 --> 01:24.210
Wrong! It's first strike wins!

01:24.210 --> 01:25.800
Make haste slowly!

01:27.650 --> 01:29.140
What's the point in spinnin'?!

01:29.350 --> 01:30.340
Beautifully!

01:30.850 --> 01:32.280
Excellent!

01:32.720 --> 01:34.880
Hey, are you listening, Mizuki?

01:35.150 --> 01:36.420
Sorry, what were you saying?

01:36.920 --> 01:39.890
Honestly! We were talking about what to do for summer break.

01:40.090 --> 01:41.460
Drill style!

01:41.460 --> 01:42.760
Summer break?

01:43.430 --> 01:46.920
Oh, but I guess we've got finals before that. What a bummer.

01:51.740 --> 01:54.500
Think about summer break!
That's your homework!

01:57.840 --> 01:59.740
I'll be handing out the results of the mock tests now.

01:59.740 --> 02:00.910
What?!

02:00.150 --> 02:02.640
Come and get them in order of attendance.

02:03.180 --> 02:04.010
Aikawa.

02:05.750 --> 02:09.310
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

02:09.820 --> 02:12.960
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

02:12.960 --> 02:16.520
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

02:16.760 --> 02:19.790
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

02:20.070 --> 02:23.770
<i>It just doesn't get across...</i>
<i>Nani o Shite mo Tsutawarazu</i>

02:23.770 --> 02:27.310
<i>It's just not working right at all.</i>
<i>Umaku Ikanai Bakari de</i>

02:27.310 --> 02:30.640
<i>But even I and everyone else...</i>
<i>Watashi Datte Dare Datte</i>

02:30.840 --> 02:34.340
<i>... have times like that.</i>
<i>Atarimae ni Aru Koto</i>

02:34.450 --> 02:37.810
<i>Those things that don't return to your heart.</i>
<i>Mune no Naka ni Kaeranai</i>

02:38.020 --> 02:41.420
<i>But even those words and feelings...</i>
<i>Omoi mo Kotoba mo Itsuka</i>

02:41.590 --> 02:45.990
<i>... will come back in time someday...</i>
<i>Jikan ga Tateba Modotte Kuru kara</i>

02:46.220 --> 02:49.130
<i>... before you know it.</i>
<i>Shiranai Uchi ni</i>

02:49.430 --> 02:55.370
<i>There's only one thing you can do right now.</i>
<i>Ima Kimiga Dekiru Koto wa Hitotsu</i>

02:55.700 --> 03:02.440
<i>Just accept it and go with it.</i>
<i>Sono Mama Ukeirete Yukou</i>

03:03.070 --> 03:07.030
<i>Just be you and stay true to yourself.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Itsuwarazu ni</i>

03:07.110 --> 03:10.250
<i>Take a little break.</i>
<i>Sukoshi Hitoyasumi Shite</i>

03:10.250 --> 03:14.020
<i>Take your impatience and your hardships...</i>
<i>Aseru Kimochi Kurushii Koto</i>

03:14.020 --> 03:17.280
<i>...and turn them into your strengths.</i>
<i>Kimi no Power ni Kaete</i>

03:17.360 --> 03:21.120
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

03:21.460 --> 03:24.600
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

03:24.600 --> 03:28.190
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

03:28.370 --> 03:31.300
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

03:34.510 --> 03:41.280
THAT'S

03:34.510 --> 03:41.280
THE

03:34.510 --> 03:41.280
PROBLEM

03:47.690 --> 03:49.420
<i>I'm sure you know who you are,</i>

03:49.420 --> 03:51.080
<i>but a lot of you are slacking off lately!</i>

03:51.590 --> 03:55.250
Don't you think you can graduate without doing anything.

03:55.390 --> 03:57.330
If you think you're one of them,

03:57.330 --> 04:00.420
buckle down and do your best on the finals! Got it?

04:02.700 --> 04:05.100
Name: Kazuki Sendou Class: 3-D
Attendance: Number 11
Previous Rank: A Standing: 41
Current Rank: D Standing: 148

04:02.700 --> 04:05.100
Mock Test Result Chart

04:09.770 --> 04:12.610
Finals are a laughable matter before our great event.

04:13.110 --> 04:15.770
But if I end up having to repeat senior year...

04:16.850 --> 04:18.440
What? Top of the class?!

04:18.680 --> 04:20.620
You can do anything if you put your mind to it!

04:20.620 --> 04:22.310
Comrade Kazuki, what is our main duty?

04:22.520 --> 04:24.820
Studying, I guess, in the end.

04:24.820 --> 04:25.820
Fool!

04:25.820 --> 04:27.950
Doujin activity, of course!

04:28.560 --> 04:31.860
But if I don't take steps like decreasing the page count,

04:31.860 --> 04:33.430
I'll end up doing bad at both.

04:33.430 --> 04:35.490
You defeatist!

04:36.000 --> 04:39.670
You think you can conquer the world with that kind of attitude?!

04:39.670 --> 04:42.040
We are doing all this now in order to cultivate...

04:42.040 --> 04:44.480
...the endurance we will need to conquer the world!

04:44.680 --> 04:46.010
Bring your thighs up higher!

04:46.010 --> 04:47.480
Come on, 1, 2! 1, 2!

04:52.320 --> 04:53.910
Oh, Sir!

04:54.920 --> 04:57.890
What is the matter?
You seem rather down.

05:00.090 --> 05:03.730
But, but, I think that just shows how hard you worked...

05:03.730 --> 05:07.220
...for the spring exhibition and spot sale, as well as at your job.

05:09.300 --> 05:11.460
Yeah, by neglecting my studies.

05:16.010 --> 05:18.310
Are you doing okay on your tests, Chisa?

05:18.880 --> 05:20.870
Yes, I am fine!

05:22.510 --> 05:23.380
I see.

05:24.050 --> 05:26.480
I guess everyone else has both sides worked out.

05:26.720 --> 05:30.260
Oh, but, but, I'm just barely getting by.

05:30.260 --> 05:32.490
I am sure you will be able to do it if you try!

05:33.290 --> 05:35.520
Of course, I can't do it if I don't try.

05:40.370 --> 05:43.730
I'll set a goal of 3 pages of layout each day.

05:44.700 --> 05:47.410
At the latest, I'll finish it by mid-July,

05:47.410 --> 05:51.340
then design the cover in parallel with studying for exams...

05:52.140 --> 05:54.910
I'll hold off on the subjects that need memorizing, so English and math...

05:54.910 --> 05:57.880
FINAL EXAMS

05:54.910 --> 05:57.880
Schedule

05:54.910 --> 05:57.880
7/10 7/11 7/12

05:54.910 --> 05:57.880
Modern Lit English Classic Lit II

05:54.910 --> 05:57.880
Math III

05:54.910 --> 05:57.880
Math C

05:54.910 --> 05:57.880
World History B

05:54.910 --> 05:57.880
Biology II

05:54.910 --> 05:57.880
Physics II

05:55.650 --> 05:57.880
It's no good! I won't have time for classic lit at this rate!

05:58.220 --> 06:01.780
I'll just have to study after
I've finished the layouts!

06:02.020 --> 06:03.220
8 pages a day!

06:07.990 --> 06:10.300
But will I really be able to do it?

06:10.300 --> 06:12.320
If I still end up with bad grades...

06:14.700 --> 06:16.220
I'll think about it at home.

06:18.270 --> 06:19.240
Mizuki?

06:20.970 --> 06:23.840
I... umbrella...

06:24.410 --> 06:25.400
Umbrella?

06:34.490 --> 06:37.320
It's been a while since
I've talked to you, Mizuki.

06:37.320 --> 06:39.520
No way! We just talked the other day!

06:39.820 --> 06:40.590
What?

06:40.860 --> 06:42.760
Remember? At your job?

06:43.260 --> 06:47.260
That doesn't really count!
You went home so quickly.

06:47.470 --> 06:49.130
Well, it can't be helped.

06:49.770 --> 06:51.960
You've been so busy lately.

06:52.300 --> 06:53.940
You're always doing something different,

06:53.940 --> 06:58.100
so it can't be helped if you think it's been a while.

06:58.240 --> 06:59.710
Or rather, it's not surprising...

07:01.780 --> 07:03.610
You sound kind of bitter.

07:04.080 --> 07:05.640
I'm not really...

07:19.800 --> 07:22.900
My grades were really bad.

07:22.900 --> 07:24.230
On the mock tests?

07:24.500 --> 07:26.370
I couldn't help but feel kind of down.

07:26.440 --> 07:28.210
You just have to work hard for next time.

07:28.210 --> 07:32.580
Well, yeah, but finals are coming up fast and I don't have time.

07:32.940 --> 07:34.680
You'll have plenty of time if you start now!

07:34.680 --> 07:35.810
We could work on it together.

07:36.080 --> 07:36.840
What?

07:37.180 --> 07:40.350
Remember? We worked on the billboard for the sports fest...

07:40.350 --> 07:41.940
...in middle school together, too!

07:42.050 --> 07:44.250
Oh, that sure was a lot of work, wasn't it?

07:45.060 --> 07:46.490
I'll help you.

07:46.720 --> 07:47.730
You, Mizuki?

07:47.730 --> 07:50.220
Th-that's right! You should be grateful!

07:50.700 --> 07:53.220
But you've never drawn a comic before, have you?

07:58.940 --> 08:00.000
I don't believe it!

08:00.000 --> 08:03.000
Why would I help you with the comic?!

08:03.540 --> 08:06.200
I'm saying I'll help you with your studies!

08:07.310 --> 08:09.440
That makes more sense.

08:10.450 --> 08:12.520
After all, you were good at all the other subjects,

08:12.520 --> 08:14.080
but you were unbelievable at art.

08:24.800 --> 08:26.030
What's with you?! What's with you?!

08:30.970 --> 08:34.340
It is impressive that you saw through my defense, my sister!

08:34.570 --> 08:36.700
What are you doing here?!

08:38.840 --> 08:40.210
Good of you to ask.

08:44.750 --> 08:46.310
What's this?

08:46.750 --> 08:48.910
Here!

08:46.750 --> 08:48.910
Orders!

08:49.120 --> 08:50.710
Go see her.

08:51.760 --> 08:54.450
Minami Makimura? Who's that?

08:56.490 --> 09:01.400
The preacher of life!
The greatest pioneer! Life advisor!

09:01.700 --> 09:03.100
Some suspicious religion?

09:04.270 --> 09:05.400
No!

09:06.800 --> 09:08.870
Those who are lost are fortunate.

09:08.870 --> 09:10.840
Seek her out and the way is sure to open up!

09:12.310 --> 09:16.300
Lay out your troubles and your reservations plainly before her,

09:16.880 --> 09:20.110
and you are certain to gain beneficial advice!

09:20.790 --> 09:24.650
Therefore, you are to head to this place at 17:00 tomorrow.

09:25.290 --> 09:27.120
I have contacted her already.
You may not cancel at the last minute.

09:27.560 --> 09:29.530
Wait...tomorrow...?

09:29.930 --> 09:31.620
You already promised her?

09:31.900 --> 09:32.590
Yes.

09:32.860 --> 09:34.700
You can't just decide these things on your own...

09:34.700 --> 09:36.790
Do not let it bother you!
Your thanks is not necessary!

09:37.030 --> 09:39.060
Well then, farewell!

09:39.540 --> 09:41.440
Hey, Taishi!

09:43.740 --> 09:45.570
H-he's gone...

10:04.160 --> 10:05.250
Hey, what's up?

10:06.260 --> 10:08.630
Say, Kazuki, what are you going to do about tomorrow?

10:08.970 --> 10:10.870
What? Oh.

10:11.470 --> 10:12.960
I'll go, probably.

10:13.140 --> 10:14.000
<i>Really?</i>

10:14.340 --> 10:17.100
Taishi said he promised already, after all,

10:17.280 --> 10:20.140
and I might be able to ask stuff about Comi-Pa, so...

10:20.550 --> 10:21.540
I see.

10:22.650 --> 10:24.950
Hey, can I come, too?

10:24.950 --> 10:25.640
<i>What?</i>

10:26.180 --> 10:28.050
I'm a little interested, so I'll come.

10:28.050 --> 10:29.490
So, I'll see you tomorrow, Kazuki!

10:31.190 --> 10:32.450
Oh, hey!

10:34.430 --> 10:36.090
What'd she mean that she's interested?

10:36.930 --> 10:40.630
What the heck, Kazuki?!
You don't even know who Maki is?!

10:41.300 --> 10:42.870
Is she famous?

10:42.870 --> 10:44.370
Of course she is!

10:44.370 --> 10:47.500
People even say she's the true person behind Comi-Pa!

10:47.840 --> 10:48.970
Wow.

10:49.240 --> 10:51.510
It's not a "wow" matter!

10:52.080 --> 10:55.250
She's well informed about various exhibition and spot sales,

10:55.250 --> 10:58.820
and she's even reorganized numerous events that had gotten in trouble...

10:58.820 --> 11:00.550
...and were on the verge of gettin' cancelled.

11:00.790 --> 11:05.810
Having Maki around is like a guarantee that your event'll succeed.

11:06.290 --> 11:08.860
She's got a great reputation, she's good at working budgets,

11:08.860 --> 11:11.560
and no one's better at directin' an event onsite!

11:12.830 --> 11:16.320
Is someone that famous really going to meet with me?

11:16.870 --> 11:18.560
Don't worry 'bout that!

11:18.870 --> 11:21.770
If you've got questions, just fire away.

11:22.040 --> 11:23.270
She's a real great person...

11:23.270 --> 11:25.270
...and she's sure to answer your questions seriously.

11:25.540 --> 11:26.740
Okay.

11:26.740 --> 11:30.450
By the way, is your manuscript comin' along okay?

11:30.450 --> 11:33.450
If you dawdle too much, Comi-Pa's gonna be here before ya know it!

11:33.450 --> 11:34.250
Yeah.

11:34.720 --> 11:36.720
I'm pretty much done with the layouts,

11:36.720 --> 11:38.710
so I'm thinkin' of startin' on the rough sketches.

11:38.960 --> 11:40.360
What?! But what about finals?

11:40.930 --> 11:41.530
I gave up!

11:41.530 --> 11:42.250
What?!

11:42.360 --> 11:43.960
Tests happen all the time,

11:43.960 --> 11:47.060
but Comi-Pa is a great event happenin' for the first time!

11:47.300 --> 11:50.600
Between finals and Comi-Pa,
I'll pick Comi-Pa!

11:50.970 --> 11:53.770
I wish I could have such total conviction.

11:53.970 --> 11:56.100
I'm so indecisive.

11:58.240 --> 11:59.770
Kazuki, you're late!

12:00.710 --> 12:02.980
You were serious about coming?

12:05.820 --> 12:08.320
Well, you never had any interest in doujinshi...

12:08.320 --> 12:09.980
...and exhibition and spot sales before...

12:10.050 --> 12:11.190
That's why!

12:11.190 --> 12:13.790
You can't trust someone that Taishi introduces!

12:13.790 --> 12:15.790
What are you going to do if they trick you or threaten you...

12:15.790 --> 12:18.020
...or make you buy some weird stuff?!

12:18.330 --> 12:20.600
They're not a corrupt business...

12:20.600 --> 12:22.360
But it's through Taishi's introduction!

12:27.570 --> 12:29.730
Zatsui Building. This is it.

12:30.910 --> 12:32.110
On the third floor.

12:32.110 --> 12:33.940
Comic Party

12:32.110 --> 12:33.940
Preparation Committee Office

12:34.380 --> 12:35.980
What's wrong? Aren't you coming?

12:35.980 --> 12:37.450
What? Yeah.

12:37.780 --> 12:41.410
You're weird. You were walking ahead of me until just now.

12:42.920 --> 12:45.320
Excuse me, please let me through.

12:45.890 --> 12:47.190
Oh, excuse me.

12:49.690 --> 12:50.750
Oh, my!

12:51.230 --> 12:52.030
Oh!

13:06.340 --> 13:07.140
Here we are.

13:08.150 --> 13:09.440
Wow!

13:10.750 --> 13:14.120
So, you're Taishi's friend!

13:14.390 --> 13:16.890
I'm sorry about what happened at the spring event.

13:16.890 --> 13:19.050
It was my first time, and I didn't know anything.

13:19.660 --> 13:23.250
I was there as extra help at that event.

13:23.690 --> 13:26.760
I never thought I would get to see you again.

13:27.130 --> 13:28.600
Could you put that down there?

13:30.670 --> 13:32.160
Are these boxes...?

13:32.470 --> 13:34.630
Applications to participate in Comi-Pa.

13:35.540 --> 13:37.700
Wow, so many?

13:38.610 --> 13:41.510
This is still only about two-thirds of it.

13:41.780 --> 13:45.480
Actually, my application should be in there somewhere, too.

13:45.850 --> 13:47.010
I see.

13:47.820 --> 13:48.510
Yes.

13:52.260 --> 13:53.390
Yes, yes.

13:53.390 --> 13:55.330
Miss Makimura, could you come here a minute?

13:56.230 --> 13:57.250
Okay!

14:00.630 --> 14:03.530
It's a phone call from the Tokyo
Convention Association.

14:03.530 --> 14:06.400
Also, the fire department asked that you contact them.

14:06.540 --> 14:08.300
I wonder if it's concerning our arrangements?

14:09.140 --> 14:12.080
I'm sorry, would you wait a little while?

14:14.980 --> 14:16.970
It looks like a normal company.

14:17.680 --> 14:18.710
Normal?

14:19.180 --> 14:20.910
I thought it'd be more weird.

14:21.790 --> 14:23.290
That's sort of rude.

14:23.290 --> 14:24.390
Well?!

14:24.390 --> 14:26.080
Shall we go out for tea?

14:26.990 --> 14:29.050
I know of a wonderful little place.

14:34.130 --> 14:37.500
Oh, wow!
They have Lapsang Souchong!

14:38.200 --> 14:39.500
What'll I do?

14:39.500 --> 14:42.740
I want to try the Imperial, but Marco Polo is a must...

14:42.940 --> 14:45.310
You like tea?

14:45.540 --> 14:47.670
Oh, well, sort of.

14:48.080 --> 14:49.170
I'm glad.

14:54.950 --> 14:56.980
I'm sorry for taking up your time when you seem so busy.

14:58.420 --> 15:02.190
It's all right.
I wanted to take a break anyway.

15:03.560 --> 15:05.620
Is it always like that?

15:06.500 --> 15:10.070
Yes, I suppose, especially right before an event.

15:10.070 --> 15:11.800
After accepting applications,

15:11.800 --> 15:14.410
there's the participating group lottery and final decisions,

15:14.410 --> 15:17.030
sending notices, making arrangements for the convention hall,

15:17.710 --> 15:20.210
contacting and negotiating with all parties involved,

15:20.210 --> 15:21.700
supervising the budget...

15:21.950 --> 15:23.540
There's a lot to do.

15:23.950 --> 15:25.040
It sounds like a lot of trouble.

15:25.320 --> 15:28.420
Yes, but I enjoy my work,

15:28.420 --> 15:31.010
so I don't feel that it's hard, even if it is.

15:32.820 --> 15:36.430
But you didn't come here to talk about finding employment...

15:36.430 --> 15:40.090
...in the preparation committee or anything like that, right, Mr. Sendou?

15:40.460 --> 15:42.190
Oh, no.

15:44.300 --> 15:47.530
I don't know if it's appropriate for me to ask this,

15:47.940 --> 15:51.900
but how were you when you were in high school, Miss Minami?

15:52.180 --> 15:54.300
What? Me?

15:54.980 --> 15:57.950
Well, what I really want to know is how you managed to balance...

15:57.950 --> 16:00.480
...your doujin work and your school work.

16:00.480 --> 16:03.350
I'm in bad shape with both right now.

16:03.820 --> 16:07.590
I'm not sure I can put out a book at this rate.

16:07.960 --> 16:12.420
Oh, but it's a rude question.
Or rather, I'm being spoiled, aren't I?

16:12.800 --> 16:13.730
I'm sorry.

16:14.100 --> 16:16.900
That sounds so wonderful!

16:17.270 --> 16:17.830
What?

16:18.140 --> 16:20.300
When I was in high school,

16:20.300 --> 16:21.970
I wouldn't have been able to participate in exhibition and spot sales,

16:21.970 --> 16:23.500
even if I wanted to.

16:23.770 --> 16:26.680
Why not? Were people around you against it?

16:27.210 --> 16:29.740
One reason was that I had no money.

16:30.080 --> 16:33.920
It's hard to work a part-time job as a high school student, you know?

16:35.550 --> 16:39.680
And there weren't any exhibition and spot sales where I'm from.

16:39.890 --> 16:42.550
So, I couldn't have participated even if I'd wanted to.

16:43.060 --> 16:44.630
Even if I put together a book,

16:44.630 --> 16:46.460
about all I could do was sell it at the school festival.

16:48.000 --> 16:51.370
So, I find your problem very envious.

16:52.570 --> 16:54.200
You're so lucky.

16:55.040 --> 16:58.030
I'm sorry. I'm asking for too much, aren't I?

16:58.310 --> 17:01.380
That's not true, because I'm the same.

17:01.380 --> 17:01.970
What?

17:02.250 --> 17:05.920
When I think about
Comic Party right now,

17:05.920 --> 17:07.710
I feel so overwhelmed.

17:11.290 --> 17:15.850
There's so much to do, I wonder if we'll really be able to hold it.

17:17.190 --> 17:20.730
At times like that, I try to think about the things I can do now...

17:20.730 --> 17:23.430
...and the things I have to take care of first.

17:24.440 --> 17:27.960
When you think about having to do this and that, it seems hard,

17:28.270 --> 17:32.470
but if you prioritize things and take care of them one by one,

17:32.910 --> 17:36.400
you'll have achieved your goal before you know it.

17:39.620 --> 17:42.880
I'm saying this partly to tell myself what I should do, though.

17:48.690 --> 17:51.560
Thank you very much for today.

17:51.560 --> 17:55.120
Not at all. I hope when we meet next time, it'll be at the convention hall.

17:56.530 --> 17:57.360
Yes.

17:57.630 --> 17:58.500
Wanna get going?

17:58.500 --> 17:59.200
Okay.

18:02.610 --> 18:04.070
She's so cool.

18:10.780 --> 18:12.270
Go on ahead.

18:13.380 --> 18:14.010
Mizuki?

18:21.460 --> 18:22.430
Miss Makimura.

18:23.530 --> 18:24.430
Oh.

18:24.660 --> 18:25.650
Um...

18:26.260 --> 18:30.100
Did you really mean it when you said you enjoyed your work?

18:30.630 --> 18:31.330
What?

18:34.270 --> 18:37.210
Haven't you lost some things along the way, too?

18:38.010 --> 18:39.500
Lost some things?

18:40.340 --> 18:42.710
Well, you're not working at a normal company...

18:43.210 --> 18:46.020
Um, and it's sort of an odd job...

18:46.020 --> 18:48.580
That is, I'm not saying you're weird, but...

18:50.020 --> 18:54.080
Did you think that what we were doing wasn't normal?

18:54.290 --> 18:54.990
What?

18:55.860 --> 18:58.020
I don't mean it like that, but...

18:58.500 --> 19:00.520
Just that, I don't quite understand it, I guess...

19:01.570 --> 19:04.470
A job where we work to bring together the sentiment of liking something.

19:04.700 --> 19:05.400
What?

19:05.800 --> 19:08.400
That's how I think of it.

19:11.040 --> 19:13.680
So, even when it's hard and it's a lot of trouble,

19:13.680 --> 19:18.240
I love this job and I intend to continue at it.

19:30.460 --> 19:32.030
<i>So, you don't have to think...</i>

19:32.030 --> 19:34.520
<i>...about drawing it well or</i> <i>trying to make it look like me.</i>

19:36.400 --> 19:37.160
No.

19:37.470 --> 19:38.630
What's wrong with this?

19:42.340 --> 19:43.830
I think it's a good drawing.

19:48.480 --> 19:49.340
Kazuki!

19:53.020 --> 19:53.750
Let's go home.

20:01.360 --> 20:03.920
What you want to do and what you ought to do, huh?

20:04.760 --> 20:07.630
All right! Today, I'm going to study for the tests!

20:08.530 --> 20:10.900
I'll move onto the manuscript after
I've properly taken care of this!

20:11.270 --> 20:11.960
Yeah.

20:12.170 --> 20:14.440
Here you go. I brought a collection of questions,

20:14.440 --> 20:15.800
so let's get cracking now!

20:20.610 --> 20:23.950
Comrade Kazuki, if you had chosen to abandon your studies...

20:23.950 --> 20:26.510
...and concentrate on your doujin work,

20:27.580 --> 20:30.350
I would have torn this up and thrown it away!

20:30.350 --> 20:33.320
Participation Registration Card

20:33.860 --> 20:36.260
Doujin work or your studies!

20:36.560 --> 20:38.190
I don't intend to demand that you choose.

20:38.430 --> 20:42.830
Why? Because choosing both is the path to world conquest!

20:48.940 --> 20:51.500
I thought I heard Taishi's voice...

20:57.510 --> 20:58.680
I must be hearing things.

21:01.050 --> 21:02.350
Is this your comic?

21:03.450 --> 21:04.150
Yeah.

21:06.120 --> 21:06.850
What do you think?

21:08.730 --> 21:10.060
I don't really know,

21:12.730 --> 21:13.960
but this is your art style, Kazuki!

21:16.630 --> 21:18.330
Yup, it hasn't changed.

21:18.470 --> 21:20.460
What the heck is that supposed to mean?

21:21.740 --> 21:22.970
I'm praising you!

21:23.740 --> 21:26.300
How is that praise?

21:31.980 --> 21:32.850
Bye!

21:35.990 --> 21:37.550
It's over!

21:38.190 --> 21:39.120
Kazuki!

21:42.530 --> 21:43.550
How did it go?

21:48.300 --> 21:49.030
V!

22:19.760 --> 22:24.000
<i>The distant sky looked bright...</i>
<i>Touku no Sora ga Akaruku Mieta</i>

22:24.000 --> 22:28.500
<i>...and we began walking.</i>
<i>Soshite Bokura wa Arukihajimeta</i>

22:28.610 --> 22:33.010
<i>Getting our feet caught in the mud.</i>
<i>Nukarumi ni Ashi o Torarenagara</i>

22:33.180 --> 22:37.080
<i>Heading for a shapeless city.</i>
<i>Katachi no Nai Machi o Mezashite</i>

22:37.080 --> 22:41.220
<i>The pocket in my heart was full...</i>
<i>Kokoro no Naka no Pocket ni wa</i>

22:41.220 --> 22:45.490
<i>...of the grownup things we'd just learned.</i>
<i>Oboetate no Otona ga Ippai</i>

22:45.660 --> 22:50.060
<i>Having taken off our uniforms...</i>
<i>Seifuku o Nuida Bokura ni wa</i>

22:50.190 --> 22:54.230
<i>... the wind was just a little too cold.</i>
<i>Kaze wa Sukoshi Tsumetasugita</i>

22:54.230 --> 22:57.770
<i>Who in the world am I?</i>
<i>Ittai Boku wa Dare Darou</i>

22:57.770 --> 23:02.710
<i>I think about that every so often.</i>
<i>Tokidoki Sonna Koto o Omou</i>

23:02.840 --> 23:06.340
<i>In the world outside the school building...</i>
<i>Kousha no Soto no Sekai de wa</i>

23:06.340 --> 23:11.780
<i>...it's like everyone is a</i> <i>pawn in a game of chess.</i>
<i>Daremo ga Marude Chess no Koma sa</i>

23:12.850 --> 23:17.320
<i>I'm here for you.</i>
<i>Kimi no Tame ni Boku ga Ite</i>

23:17.320 --> 23:21.330
<i>And you for me.</i>
<i>Boku no Tame ni Kimiga</i>

23:21.330 --> 23:25.860
<i>When you think about that...</i>
<i>Sou Omoeba Daremo ga</i>

23:25.860 --> 23:34.830
<i>... everyone is needed by someone.</i>
<i>Dareka no Tame ni Hitsuyou sa</i>

23:55.460 --> 24:19.780
PREVIEW

23:57.190 --> 23:59.230
Kazuki has his eyes set on Comic Party.

23:59.760 --> 24:01.630
He goes out on a date with Mizuki,

24:01.630 --> 24:03.700
but he cannot even focus on having fun.

24:04.170 --> 24:09.370
However, due to his zeal, he falls into a terrible trap.

24:09.770 --> 24:12.840
What's going on, Taishi?
You're so normal today.

24:13.080 --> 24:15.310
We received claims for compensation from various places...

24:15.310 --> 24:17.050
...saying that the previews weren't really previews.

24:17.050 --> 24:19.080
I see. Well, that isn't surprising.

24:20.280 --> 24:22.820
Next time, "Onward to Comic Party!"

24:20.280 --> 24:26.120
NEXT TIME

24:20.280 --> 24:26.120
ONWARD TO

24:20.280 --> 24:26.120
COMIC PARTY!
